Fillets: an OnSame end whose face at the end lies on a trimmed surface
crossed by the opposite contact only past its bounds (mitcad#236).

A plate's bottom edge is rounded with 3 up to a conical foot below the
plate (the foot's rim on the plate's bottom, the cone cut flush with the
plate's side). At the edge's end the cone is the face at the end (OnSame):
the corner intersects the opposite contact, on the side 3 above the
bottom, with the face at the end extended, and caps the blend with its
intersection with that face, the cone/side edge prolonged up to the cap.
The cone continued above its rim crosses the side's contact before the
edge's end, but stored bodies carry the cone on a surface trimmed at the
face's bounds (Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface); ChFi3d_ExtendSurface
extends only B-spline and Bezier surfaces, so the intersection was sought
on the cone below its rim, found nothing, and the corner failed ("OneCorner
: bouchon non ecrit"). The same body with an untrimmed cone builds.

Where that intersection fails, ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner now tries
the face at the end extended as its basis surface is
(ChFi3d_UntrimmedEndSurface: an elementary basis, unbounded where it is not
periodic, one period from the trimmed start where it is, so that the face's
own curves keep their parameters). When the contact meets it there, the cap
and the prolonged edge are built on it; the face keeps its surface (a new
surface given to the face lost the second p-curve of its seam in the
topological build), its new curves lying past the trimmed bounds on the
same parameters. Where the trimmed surface is crossed, nothing changes.
